@startuml Preciazo_DB_Shopping_Planning

title Preciazo - Shopping Planning Database Diagram

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

entity shopping_lists {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    owner_id : BIGINT <<REF>>
    name : VARCHAR
    currency : VARCHAR
    status : VARCHAR
    created_at : TIMESTAMP
}

entity shopping_list_members {
    * shopping_list_id : BIGINT <<PK, FK>>
    * user_id : BIGINT <<PK, REF>>
    --
    member_role : VARCHAR
}

entity shopping_list_items {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    shopping_list_id : BIGINT <<FK>>
    product_id : BIGINT <<REF>>
    requested_name : VARCHAR
    quantity : DECIMAL
    quantity_unit : VARCHAR
    estimated_unit_price : DECIMAL
    price_currency : VARCHAR
    price_per_quantity : DECIMAL
    price_per_unit : VARCHAR
    purchased : BOOLEAN
}

entity purchase_budgets {
    * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
    --
    shopping_list_id : BIGINT <<FK, UQ>>
    amount : DECIMAL
    currency : VARCHAR
}

shopping_lists ||--o{ shopping_list_members
shopping_lists ||--o{ shopping_list_items
shopping_lists ||--o| purchase_budgets

note right of shopping_lists
  owner_id and member user_id belong to
  Identity and Access.
end note

note right of shopping_list_items
  product_id belongs to
  Catalog and Pricing.
end note

note right of purchase_budgets
  UNIQUE(shopping_list_id): one optional budget per list.
  amount > 0; currency matches shopping_lists.currency.
  Changing the budget updates its limit; invalid input is rejected.
  Totals and budget warnings are derived on query, not stored.
  Warning: defined limit AND projected total > limit.
  Clear warning at or below the limit; no warning event is stored.
end note

note bottom of shopping_list_items
  UNIQUE(shopping_list_id, product_id).
  Adding an existing product increases quantity without a duplicate.
  quantity > 0; price_per_quantity > 0; estimated_unit_price >= 0.
  Quantity and price units must be compatible; price currency matches the list.
  Subtotal = estimated_unit_price * quantity / price_per_quantity
  after converting quantity to price_per_unit.
  Projected total sums all subtotals; checkout total sums purchased items only.
  Unmarking sets purchased = false and reduces checkout total on the next query.
end note

@enduml
